Interactive edits of the arnold primvars of a camera whose Hydra 2 prim only has them in its primvars container

A grey sphere is seen by a camera whose primvars:arnold:exposure goes from 0 to 4 and back, the stage being
re-rendered after each edit, with the HdArnoldRendererPlugin render delegate driven like a Hydra host, see
testsuite/common/interactive_usd_test.h. In the Hydra 2 mode, a scene index filter makes the camera prim look like
the ones of MayaHydra: the camera schema only holds its own fields, and the arnold primvar is in the primvars
container as "arnold:exposure". The render delegate must read it from there, as GetCameraParamValue doesn't find it.
As with MayaHydra, an edit of the exposure only dirties that primvar, not the camera schema: the arnold scene index
plugins must dirty the camera schema for the camera to be synced.
Each render is checked in test.cpp, and the overexposed render is compared against the reference image.

author: sebastien.blaineau.ortega@autodesk.com

PARAMS: {'program_env': 'interactive_usd'}
